# Sync Echo Elimination — Implementation Walkthrough

## Problem
After a **Push (PUT)**, the server returns only `{"updated": 2, "skipped": [], "errors": 0}`. The App doesn't know the server-generated `updated_at`, so the next **Pull (GET)** re-downloads the same records. The App ignores them via hash check, but this wastes bandwidth.

## Solution
Return server-generated metadata (`id`, `updated_at`, `server_hash`) immediately in the Push response. The App then updates its local Hive records and advances the watermark, so the next Pull skips those records entirely.

